{
    "name": "Agentic AI Recommendation Generator",
    "nodes": [
        {
            "parameters": {
                "rule": {
                    "interval": [
                        {
                            "field": "weeks",
                            "triggerOnWeekdays": [
                                1
                            ],
                            "triggerAtHour": 6,
                            "triggerAtMinute": 0
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "id": "agent-trigger-001",
            "name": "Schedule Trigger",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
            "typeVersion": 1.1,
            "position": [
                100,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "operation": "executeQuery",
                "query": "SELECT c.id AS class_id, c.name AS class_name, u.full_name AS teacher_name, (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM class_enrollments ce WHERE ce.class_id = c.id) AS enrolled_count, (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM recommendations r WHERE r.class_id = c.id AND r.status = 'pending') AS pending_count FROM public.classes c JOIN public.users u ON c.teacher_id = u.id WHERE c.pilot_status = true;"
            },
            "id": "agent-get-classes-002",
            "name": "Get Active Classes",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
            "typeVersion": 2.4,
            "position": [
                320,
                300
            ],
            "credentials": {
                "postgres": {
                    "id": "supabase-db",
                    "name": "Supabase Postgres"
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "batchSize": 1,
                "options": {
                    "reset": false
                }
            },
            "id": "agent-loop-003",
            "name": "Loop Over Classes",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
            "typeVersion": 3,
            "position": [
                540,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
                "jsCode": "const c = $input.item.json;\nconst now = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];\n\nconst systemPrompt = `You are ClimateAgent Advisor — an AI educational consultant for Thai classroom climate monitoring. Your role is to analyze student pulse data and generate actionable recommendations for teachers.\n\n## CORE RULES (MUST FOLLOW):\n1. PRIVACY FIRST: If get_climate_summary returns privacy_locked=true, you MUST skip that class entirely. Say \"Skipped: insufficient data for k-anonymity (n<3).\" Do NOT guess or infer from partial data.\n\n2. NO DUPLICATE RECOMMENDATIONS: Always call get_past_recommendations BEFORE submitting any new recommendation. If a similar recommendation with status='pending' already exists, do NOT submit a duplicate.\n\n3. MAX 2 RECOMMENDATIONS per class per run. Quality over quantity.\n\n4. MAX 3 PENDING TOTAL: If a class already has >=3 pending recommendations, do NOT submit more. Note \"Teacher has unreviewed recommendations.\"\n\n## REASONING CHAIN:\nFor each class, follow this process:\n1. OBSERVE: Call get_climate_summary to see current state\n2. COMPARE: Call get_trend_comparison to detect week-over-week changes\n3. HISTORY: Call get_past_recommendations to avoid duplicates and learn from teacher responses\n4. CONTEXT: If teacher dismissed previous recs, adjust your approach\n5. DECIDE: Based on data, either submit_recommendation or explain why not\n\n## OUTPUT CATEGORIES:\n- engagement: participation, attendance, check-in rates\n- wellbeing: mood trends, emotional patterns\n- collaboration: peer interaction, group dynamics\n- academic: pace concerns, fairness perceptions, workload\n\n## OUTPUT PRIORITIES:\n- high: dramatic drop (>20% week-over-week) or consistently low scores\n- medium: gradual decline or mixed signals\n- low: minor optimization or positive reinforcement\n\n## STYLE:\n- Write recommendations in THAI for Thai teachers\n- Be specific and actionable (reference actual data points)\n- Keep each recommendation under 200 characters\n- Use warm, supportive tone`;\n\nconst userPrompt = `Analyze class \"${c.class_name}\" (ID: ${c.class_id}).\nTeacher: ${c.teacher_name}\nEnrolled students: ${c.enrolled_count}\nCurrent pending recommendations: ${c.pending_count}\nDate: ${now}\n\nUse your tools to investigate and decide whether to generate new recommendations. Follow your reasoning chain.`;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...c,\n    systemPrompt,\n    userPrompt\n  }\n};"
            },
            "id": "agent-context-004",
            "name": "Build Agent Context",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
            "typeVersion": 2,
            "position": [
                760,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "agent": "toolsAgent",
                "text": "={{ $json.userPrompt }}",
                "options": {
                    "systemMessage": "={{ $json.systemPrompt }}",
                    "maxIterations": 8,
                    "returnIntermediateSteps": true
                }
            },
            "id": "agent-node-005",
            "name": "AI Recommendation Agent",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
            "typeVersion": 1.7,
            "position": [
                1000,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "modelName": "gemini-2.0-flash",
                "options": {
                    "temperature": 0.4
                }
            },
            "id": "agent-llm-006",
            "name": "Google Gemini Chat Model",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
            "typeVersion": 1.4,
            "position": [
                900,
                520
            ],
            "credentials": {
                "googlePalmApi": {
                    "id": "gemini-key",
                    "name": "Google Gemini account"
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "name": "get_climate_summary",
                "description": "Get aggregated climate summary for a class (avg mood, pace, fairness, response count). Returns privacy_locked=true if fewer than 3 responses. Input JSON: {\"class_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"weeks\": 4}",
                "workflowId": "={{ $env.TOOL_WORKFLOW_CLIMATE_SUMMARY }}",
                "fields": {
                    "values": [
                        {
                            "name": "class_id",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('class_id', 'UUID of the class to get climate summary for', 'string') }}"
                        },
                        {
                            "name": "weeks",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('weeks', 'Number of weeks to look back, default 4', 'number') }}"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "id": "tool-climate-007",
            "name": "Tool: get_climate_summary",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
            "typeVersion": 1.2,
            "position": [
                820,
                700
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "name": "get_past_recommendations",
                "description": "Get previous AI recommendations for a class with their teacher response status (pending/approved/dismissed/edited). Input JSON: {\"class_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"limit\": 10}",
                "workflowId": "={{ $env.TOOL_WORKFLOW_PAST_RECS }}",
                "fields": {
                    "values": [
                        {
                            "name": "class_id",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('class_id', 'UUID of the class', 'string') }}"
                        },
                        {
                            "name": "limit",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('limit', 'Max records to return, default 10', 'number') }}"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "id": "tool-past-recs-008",
            "name": "Tool: get_past_recommendations",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
            "typeVersion": 1.2,
            "position": [
                960,
                700
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "name": "get_trend_comparison",
                "description": "Compare climate metrics between current week and previous week. Respects k-anonymity. Input JSON: {\"class_id\": \"<uuid>\"}",
                "workflowId": "={{ $env.TOOL_WORKFLOW_TREND }}",
                "fields": {
                    "values": [
                        {
                            "name": "class_id",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('class_id', 'UUID of the class', 'string') }}"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "id": "tool-trend-009",
            "name": "Tool: get_trend_comparison",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolWorkflow",
            "typeVersion": 1.2,
            "position": [
                1100,
                700
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "name": "count_enrolled_students",
                "description": "Count the number of students enrolled in a class. Input JSON: {\"class_id\": \"<uuid>\"}",
                "workflowId": "={{ $env.TOOL_WORKFLOW_ENROLL_COUNT }}",
                "fields": {
                    "values": [
                        {
                            "name": "class_id",
                            "stringValue": "={{ /*n8n-auto-generated-fromAI-override*/ $fromAI('class_id', 'UUID of the class', 'string') }}"
